{"type": "thinking", "text": "Order: Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures.\n\nInsertion order was Alpha (1st), Beta (2nd), Audiobooks (3rd). The displayed order is alphabetical (Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta) — NOT insertion order. So the changed claim \"entries are now ordered by when they were added\" is violated: audiobooks was added last but appears between Alpha and Beta, i.e., alphabetical sorting.\n\nWait — but are these \"bookmarks\"? The drawer shows Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta, DCIM, Download... Yes these are the bookmark entries (with pencil edit icons). Since Audiobooks was added third (after Alpha, Beta) and appears second, the list is alphabetically sorted, not by addition time.\n\nHmm, but maybe \"ordered by when they were added\" means sorted ascending by insertion? No: insertion would be Alpha, Beta, Audiobooks. We got Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta. So it's alphabetical. That's a bug relative to the changed item.\n\nBut hold on — maybe these drawer folders aren't bookmarks but \"home\" shortcuts? The pencil icon suggests bookmarks editing (\"Bookmarks\" in Amaze). In Amaze, the drawer shows \"Bookmarks\" section with entries (default: DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures) and each has edit pencil. Yes, those are bookmarks. And \"Add to Bookmarks\" adds them. So indeed bookmarks list is alphabetical, not addition-ordered.\n\nHmm, but wait. Could the ordering be \"by when added\" ascending but the app records them oddly? Alpha added first, Beta second, Audiobooks third. Displayed Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta. So Audiobooks moved ahead of Beta. That's definitely not addition order.\n\nUnless adding Audiobooks didn't actually add it as a new bookmark but edited... no, Audiobooks wasn't there before.\n\nSo this is a bug: bookmarks ordered alphabetically rather than by addition time.\n\nBut let me double-check by adding another bookmark that would be out of alphabetical order, e.g., \"Alarms\" (added 4th, alphabetically before Alpha). If alphabetical, it appears first; if insertion, last. Let's do it to confirm. Also I want to check \"Beta\" -> maybe persistence across restart.\n\nLet me add Alarms bookmark. Close drawer, tap Alarms context. Actually drawer covers; tap outside to close, then root list Alarms context icon (element 10)."}
