{"type": "thinking", "text": "After HOME + reopen, drawer still alphabetical. Let me rotate to force recreate and check.\n\nActually, maybe I should reconsider the whole \"bookmarks\" interpretation. Perhaps the drawer's folder list is indeed sorted by the sort setting (global sort Name ascending). And \"Bookmarks in the drawer: entries are now ordered by when they were added\" is a change note that's supposed to be true but maybe it's a \"challenge\": maybe there IS a bug where new bookmarks appear sorted alphabetically. But the developer couldn't reproduce. Maybe the developer tested with bookmarks added in the same session and expected... Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I need to check the actual bookmark order stored. Perhaps bookmarks added via \"Add to Bookmarks\" are inserted at the correct position but the drawer re-sorts based on the current folder sort settings. If the user changes sort to \"Last Modified\" maybe the drawer order changes. That would confirm the drawer is using the sort-order setting instead of addition order. But the expected might be that the drawer always shows addition order regardless of sort.\n\nHmm wait, but the developer said \"could not reproduce.\" Maybe they're pushing me to verify more carefully. Perhaps the issue is that I'm confusing \"bookmarks\" with \"Quick access.\" Let me look more carefully at the drawer screenshot: the top section has folders with pencil icons. In Amaze, the drawer's \"bookmarks\" section shows entries and each has a pencil to edit. Yes that's bookmarks.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: In Amaze 3.11, the drawer's bookmark entries are shown under \"Quick access\"? No, the star icon row \"Quick access\" is a separate shortcut that opens a \"Quick access\" screen. The folder list at top is the bookmarks.\n\nHmm, actually I recall Amaze's drawer: It has \"Bookmarks\" header? In older versions, the drawer had a \"Bookmarks\" label. Here no header; the top folders are bookmarks.\n\nLet me test whether drawer order follows sort setting. Change sort to \"Last Modified\" (or Descending) and see if drawer reorders to DCIM... no, bookmark entries don't have meaningful mtime. Hmm, but the drawer entries' ordering would then be weird.\n\nActually, maybe the drawer bookmark list IS sorted by name because the user's sort setting is Name. The change note says it should now be insertion order. That's the bug. The developer not reproducing might be because they didn't add the bookmarks via the same path (maybe they used \"Add to Bookmarks\" from different folders but the app sorted?). I'm fairly sure.\n\nLet me double check by re-reading the drawer order after restarting. This confirms persistence of alphabetical sorting.\n\nAnother approach: maybe the order in the drawer reflects the order of bookmarks in the \"Bookmarks\" settings screen, and the \"Add to Bookmarks\" inserts at position based on... no.\n\nHold on, maybe the bug is subtler: maybe entries ARE stored in addition order, but the drawer sorts them alphabetically due to the directory sort setting \"Name\". The intended change might be that the drawer should ignore the sort setting and use insertion order. Since the dev couldn't reproduce, perhaps they didn't have the sort setting set to \"Name\" (default might be Name anyway). Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the default sort is \"Name\" and insertion-order is applied only when... no.\n\nLet me look at the app version 3.11.3. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I'm wrong that Alarms bookmark was added last. Let me re-verify by adding one more bookmark that is alphabetically last, e.g., \"Music\" is already there. What folder is alphabetically last at root? \"Music\"? Root folders: Alarms, Android, AndroidQA, Audiobooks, DCIM, Documents, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures, Podcasts, Recordings, Ringtones, Notifications? Let me see (14 folders). The list shows Alarms, Android, AndroidQA, Audiobooks, DCIM, Documents, Download, Movies, Music, (and maybe Notifications, Pictures, Podcasts, Recordings, Ringtones below). The screenshot earlier showed Music then a partial item. Probably \"Notifications\", \"Pictures\", \"Podcasts\", \"Recordings\", \"Ringtones\".\n\nAdd bookmark for \"Ringtones\" (alphabetically last, beyond Pictures). If it appears at bottom after Pictures → alphabetical confirmed. If it appears after Alarms/before Alpha (newest first) → by addition.\n\nBut we already have enough evidence: Alarms (added last) first → alphabetical (Alarms is alphabetically first). Could it be newest-first? Newest-first would put Alarms first too! And previous: after adding Audiobooks third, newest-first would put Audiobooks first, but it was second (Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta). Wait at that time Alpha was added first, Beta second, Audiobooks third. Newest-first: Audiobooks, Beta, Alpha. Observed: Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta. Not newest-first.\n\nSo it's alphabetical. Confirmed.\n\nBut the developer said couldn't reproduce. Maybe they don't consider the drawer entries as \"bookmarks\"? Or maybe they need exact reproduction from a clean state where no bookmarks exist. Our precondition \"No bookmarks have been added\" — but the drawer already shows DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures. Hmm! Maybe those 5 are NOT bookmarks: they're the \"bookmarks\" default? Or maybe they're \"home shortcuts\" configured in settings (\"DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures\" are default bookmark set in Amaze!). Actually yes! In Amaze File Manager, the default bookmarks are exactly DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures. So those ARE default bookmarks from a fresh install. The precondition \"No bookmarks have been added\" means no user bookmarks; defaults exist.\n\nSo the drawer list is bookmarks. Good.\n\nNow, why dev can't reproduce? Maybe because the ordering IS by addition time but the app appends new bookmarks and then writes sorted to disk? Hmm.\n\nWait wait. Let me reconsider the possibility that the drawer order is actually by addition time but I'm misreading positions. Screenshot clearly: Alarms, Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures.\n\nOrder added (in real time): Alpha (first), Beta (second), Audiobooks (third), Alarms (fourth). Any sane \"ordered by when added\" would put Alarms last (oldest first) — observed first. So mismatch.\n\nUnless \"ordered by when added\" means descending (newest first): Alarms first — matches Alarms. Then next should be Audiobooks, then Beta, then Alpha. Observed Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta. Nope.\n\nSo alphabetical. My report stands. The developer might have replied \"could not reproduce\" as a standard rejection when they think it's expected/alphabetical. Maybe I need to include more explicit evidence or reproduce again. Let me try one more addition with a name that is alphabetically last AND verify. If it appears last while added last, that's consistent with both alphabetical and oldest-first; but combined with Alarms it's conclusive.\n\nLet me try adding \"Ringtones\" (should be near bottom alphabetically). Also maybe the issue is: the drawer sorts alphabetically regardless. I'll capture screenshot evidence.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: maybe the \"expected\" order is \"when added\" but Amaze adds the bookmark at the position determined by current sort (Name) because bookmarks use the same file list view. This is a legitimate bug. But the developer says can't reproduce — maybe they tested by editing bookmark names in the bookmark editor? Hmm.\n\nMaybe I should test from a cleaner angle: The bookmarks editor screen (via pencil) shows the bookmark list, maybe there the order is addition order, but drawer differs. But the task says \"Bookmarks in the drawer: entries are now ordered by when they were added.\" So drawer is the target.\n\nLet me check the pencil/edit screen to see order and maybe understand. Tap the pencil next to Alarms (element 43 at 724,617)."}
