t the correct place based on addition order. The current behavior sorts by name. That's the bug. But dev said can't reproduce...\n\nMaybe the dev tested by adding bookmarks where alphabetical == addition order (e.g., added in alphabetical order). If they added in alphabetical order, they'd see \"correct\" order. That's plausible! To reproduce, additions must be out of alphabetical order. My steps do say add Alpha, Beta, Audiobooks, Alarms. Hmm, but the dev may not have done exactly.\n\nWait, actually maybe my observed order isn't alphabetical but something else? Let's double check: Alarms, Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures. Alphabetical case-insensitive: Alarms, Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta, DCIM,... Yes \"Alarms\" < \"Alpha\"? Compare \"Ala\" vs \"Alp\": 'a' < 'p' yes. Good.\n\nHmm, so I'm confident it's name-sorted, likely because drawer uses the same sort setting. Let me test changing sort to descending and see if drawer reverses. That would strengthen evidence: if drawer list follows sort setting (Name descending), then bookmark order is not addition-based at all.\n\nLet me dismiss properties, close drawer, set Sort Name Descending, then open drawer."}
