ingtones then AndroidQA. That would be very clear. But note there are already bookmarks; positions matter.\n\nActually we have enough. But let me consider: maybe dev can't reproduce because the bug only appears when bookmarks are added through the folder context menu \"Add to Bookmarks\"? That's what I did. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe I should check whether the bookmarks are being sorted by name because of an app setting \"Sort bookmarks alphabetically\" — not relevant.\n\nAlternatively, maybe my report's element_ref/quote was wrong (element 48 = Audiobooks). The developer might have rejected due to the quote not showing the defect. Hmm, \"could not reproduce\" is a reproduction issue, not quote.\n\nLet me re-file more precisely, but first let me make the reproduction cleaner: Remove the custom bookmarks Alpha, Beta, Audiobooks, Alarms? That's optional. But to make steps unambiguous, I can test adding \"Ringtones\" (5th) and \"AndroidQA\" (6th) in that order, and observe AndroidQA appears before Ringtones — clearly alphabetical, since addition order was Ringtones then AndroidQA.\n\nWait current custom additions: Alpha, Beta, Audiobooks, Alarms. That's already clear (Alarms added last appears first).\n\nHmm, maybe the problem is the dev has a different build. But instructions say keep testing same build and confirmed reports are logged. A rejection means not confirmed. I could try once more with stronger evidence and precise steps. If rejected again, maybe accept and move on? But signing off with a bug is bad. Let me try again with more detailed steps and quote the full visible order.\n\nActually, maybe I should reconsider the semantics: \"ordered by when they were added\" — perhaps in the app's bookmark data, the default bookmarks (DCIM etc.) were added at install time in the order DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures. New bookmarks might be appended after those, e.g., Alpha, Beta, Audiobooks, Alarms AFTER Pictures. But we see custom ones BEFORE DCIM. So clearly the drawer sorts by something (name) ignoring add time.\n\nAlternatively maybe the drawer sorts bookmarks that are \"directories in the current directory\"? No.\n\nHmm, one more idea: maybe the drawer lists bookmarks sorted by name because the default bookmarks list got re-sorted at startup; but the \"changed\" behavior might be about the bookmark *editor* order. The dev may have implemented ordering in the data and the drawer reads a different sorted view.\n\nLet me look for a \"Bookmarks\" management screen. Perhaps there's a \"Settings > Bookmarks\" or long-press drawer bookmark. The pencil icon opens properties. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the \"Add to Bookmarks\" dialog allows naming. Anyway.\n\nI'll re-file with precise reproduction and the full order, emphasizing out-of-order addition. Let me first restore the sort to ascending to keep data default? The sort setting is root-specific or global? We changed root's sort to descending. I'll restore later. Actually, sort is probably global (Only this folder unchecked earlier when we set Amaze descending). Hmm, we set Amaze descending with checkbox unchecked, then set Amaze ascending. Now root descending. I should restore root to ascending at the end.\n\nLet me refile the bookmark bug now with clearer evidence."}
