{"type": "thinking", "text": "Quick access screen is empty (\"No Files\"). That's a different feature (quick access files). So bookmarks are drawer folder list.\n\nHmm. So my bookmark report was rejected twice. Maybe the dev knows the behavior. Perhaps the \"ordered by when added\" is expected but the app sorts by name because that's what the build does? The dev rejected => maybe the actual expected is different.\n\nWait — maybe the bug is that the drawer bookmark order is alphabetical because we have sort By Name ascending, and the intended \"ordered by when added\" only works for *new bookmarks added after* ... no.\n\nLet me think about what \"ordered by when they were added\" could mean in terms of visible order: perhaps the newest bookmark should be at the BOTTOM of the list (appended). Our observed newest (Alarms) at top. If stored order is insertion (Alpha, Beta, Audiobooks, Alarms) then displayed reversed, we'd see Alarms, Audiobooks, Beta, Alpha. Not observed.\n\nUnless the bookmarks are stored sorted by name (Amaze bookmark storage is a map?). In Amaze, bookmarks are stored in a `Bookmarks` class with a TreeMap? Actually I recall Amaze's bookmarks are stored in a `HashMap<String, String>` in preferences and displayed... sorted. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the change intended to switch from sorted to insertion order but the dev's reply says can't reproduce because I'm misreading. Let me re-examine actual screenshot once more very carefully, maybe the order is different from my interpretation. Screenshot: Internal Storage; then Alarms, Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures. Definitely alphabetical.\n\nHmm, but wait: is it possible that the entries \"Alarms, Alpha, Audiobooks, Beta\" are NOT bookmarks I added but *sorted folder suggestions from the current directory* (root)? The drawer top list might show current directory folders? No — earlier when in Amaze dir, the drawer showed Alpha, Beta, DCIM, Download... The DCIM/Download/Movies/Music/Pictures are root folders; Alpha/Beta are Amaze subfolders. So it's a mix of my bookmarks + default bookmarks.\n\nBut wait — when we were in Amaze dir before adding any bookmark, the drawer showed DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures (not Amaze's Alpha/Beta). After adding Alpha & Beta bookmarks, they appeared. So yes, the list is the bookmarks.\n\nGiven two rejections, maybe I should try a different reproduction: maybe bookmark ordering only breaks when adding many bookmarks of a certain type, or the intended order is \"most recently added first\"? Our observed contradicts both.\n\nHold on, maybe the dev is auto-replying \"could not reproduce\" for any report whose element_ref/quote doesn't match, i.e., the quote \"Alarms\" is present but that's not the defect. The instructions say \"a quote that was never on screen gets the report rejected\". \"Alarms\" is on screen. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the issue is that element_ref 48 in the drawer observation corresponds to a LinearLayoutCompat containing \"Nov 14 | 6:33 AM\" | \"Audiobooks\" — but that's actually the drawer row for... hmm, the drawer row text from accessibility merges with underlying list. Not a big deal.\n\nLet me consider the possibility that the developer is testing \"bookmarks ordered by when added\" and it actually works in their build, meaning my observed alphabetical order is expected because the bookmarks are sorted by name due to *the file list sort setting*... but the change is about the bookmarks *editor* (maybe a \"Bookmarks\" screen accessible elsewhere).\n\nMaybe there's a dedicated bookmarks manager: long-press a bookmark in the drawer? Let me long-press a drawer bookmark row to see options (Edit/Delete/Sort?). Maybe the drawer rows support drag to reorder!\n\nLet me long-press Alpha bookmark row in drawer. But first navigate back to root.\n\nActually, maybe the bookmarks order can be changed by drag. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively maybe \"Add to Bookmarks\" from context menu adds the bookmark at an index based on time, but the drawer loader sorts. The dev may have tested by restarting and seeing... \n\nI think I should try a cleaner test: delete all custom bookmarks, then add two in reverse alphabetical order, and observe. But if the dev can't reproduce even with existing defaults, hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the bug is different: maybe the order should be by added time but the app sorts alphabetically ONLY for bookmarks whose \"sort\" was set... Since the reviewer rejected, perhaps I misidentified which screen. Let me look at the app for a \"Bookmarks\" management UI. Maybe in Settings there's \"Bookmarks\". Or maybe long-pressing the drawer's bookmark row shows \"Edit bookmark\". Let's explore the pencil icon → earlier it opened Properties for Internal Storage. Maybe for folder bookmarks the pencil opens an edit dialog. Let me try the pencil on Alpha.\n\nI'm in Quick access screen. Let me go back, open drawer, tap the pencil next to Alpha (element 47 at 724,914)."}
