{"type": "thinking", "text": "After rotation, Amaze is now in LIST view (RelativeLayout), losing the previously-set grid! That's a bug: the per-folder view setting is lost on rotation (or the activity recreation resets it).\n\nWait, but was Amaze's grid setting stored? Earlier we set Amaze grid, navigated away/back and it persisted within the session (in-memory). After rotation (activity recreate), it reverted to list. Hmm, but that could mean the setting isn't persisted to disk at all, only in memory. However, the change says \"stored per folder path\" — it should persist across rotation/restart.\n\nBut hold on: maybe the grid setting was never saved because the app saves onPause? Rotation triggers onSaveInstanceState but maybe it's stored in a static map that survives? It's lost, so maybe not.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the issue is: after rotation, Amaze reverted to list because the landscape dual-pane view forced list and then rotation back read that as the folder setting? Hmm.\n\nLet me verify: open the menu in Amaze now — does it show \"Grid View\" (meaning currently list) or \"List View\" (meaning currently grid)? It shows list layout, so menu should show \"Grid View\" (action to switch to grid). Let me check.\n\nThis is potentially the hidden bug for directory view: list/grid preference not persisted across activity recreation/config change. But wait, the change says stored per folder path — maybe it's stored in SharedPreferences and restored. Losing on rotation is a bug.\n\nBut I need to determine: is it really lost, or did the app's view mode get reset because we were in landscape and the landscape layout is list-only? On returning to portrait it should restore grid if stored. It didn't. Let me test more carefully: re-set Amaze to grid, rotate, check.\n\nAlso test app restart (HOME + open_app). If grid is lost after restart, that's a persistence bug. But the earlier HOME+open_app (from drawer/root) preserved... we didn't check grid after that.\n\nLet me be systematic:\n\n1. In Amaze, switch to grid.\n2. Open menu → confirm \"List View\" shown.\n3. Press BACK to AndroidQA (list) and re-enter Amaze → does it remain grid? (session persistence)\n4. Rotate landscape→portrait → check.\n5. HOME → open_app → check.\n\nLet me first switch Amaze to grid. Open more options."}
