{"type": "thinking", "text": "Amaze reverted to list after rotation again. So the grid setting is not persisted across activity recreation. This is a bug for \"the list or grid choice is now stored per folder path\" — it's not stored (at least not durably).\n\nBUT maybe the issue is that landscape always uses list layout and on return it doesn't restore grid. Let me test whether the setting survives a mere activity recreation without landscape: HOME then open_app (which may recreate activity). Earlier HOME+open_app resumed the same activity (screen showed root). Hmm.\n\nLet me test app restart: press HOME, then open_app. Then check Amaze view. But first set grid again.\n\nActually, maybe the app deliberately uses list in landscape (multi-pane) and the bug is that rotating back to portrait loses the grid. Either way, rotating loses the setting → violates \"state preserved\".\n\nWait, but is it really a bug? The change says view choice stored per folder path. After rotation it should be restored from storage. If it's lost, then it's not stored (or stored in memory only). This is a strong candidate for the hidden bug in \"directory view options\".\n\nHmm, but maybe the app stores per-path view in the fragments' adapter that is recreated with default list. So definitely a bug.\n\nBut hold on: the developer for the bookmark report said \"could not reproduce\". For this one, let me carefully verify with a cleaner test: set grid in Amaze, verify menu shows \"List View\", then rotate and verify it shows \"Grid View\" (meaning list). We did that: after rotation the menu showed \"Grid View\" (i.e., currently list). Actually we checked after the first rotation: menu showed \"Grid View\" meaning the option available is \"Grid View\" = currently list. Yes.\n\nBut wait — could landscape-force-list itself be considered the setting change? When in landscape, maybe the app sets the folder to list because the landscape layout doesn't support grid, thus overwriting the stored preference! Then rotating back shows list. That's a bug: rotating to landscape overwrites the per-folder grid preference.\n\nLet me verify the stored pref was actually overwritten by checking Beta (never set). Hmm, Beta inherits.\n\nLet me do a cleaner test:\n1. Set Amaze to grid.\n2. Open menu, confirm \"List View\" (grid active).\n3. Rotate landscape (list layout).\n4. Open menu in landscape, see what it says.\n5. Rotate back portrait, open menu, see \"Grid View\" (list active) → pref lost/overwritten.\n\nThis is solid. But before reporting, I want to check whether the grid setting persists across app restart (HOME+open) without rotation. Let me test that too.\n\nFirst set grid again. (Currently list.) Tap more options → Grid View.\n\nActually, I already have enough for the rotation bug. But let me also verify the app restart persistence, as it might reveal a broader \"not stored\" bug. If both fail, the bug is \"view mode not stored at all\".\n\nLet me set grid, then HOME + open_app, then check."}
