{"type": "thinking", "text": "In landscape the menu shows \"Grid View\" (meaning currently list). So as soon as we rotated to landscape, the app treats current view as list. And when we rotate back, it stays list. This means the grid preference is lost on rotation.\n\nWait, alternatively, when it rotated to landscape the app recreated the activity and read the saved preference for this folder, which apparently is list — meaning the grid choice was never saved to persistent storage at all. But then how did it persist across BACK navigation within portrait? Because it's in memory in a static/singleton map, not persisted to SharedPreferences until some save event? Hmm.\n\nEither way, the user-facing bug: After setting a folder to Grid View, rotating the device resets that folder to List View. This directly contradicts \"list or grid choice is now stored per folder path.\"\n\nLet me also test app process restart. HOME+open_app doesn't kill the process. Task switching vs killing. I can't force stop without adb. But rotation is enough.\n\nHmm, but wait: maybe the intended design is that the per-folder view mode is a \"portrait vs landscape\" separate setting, and landscape always list is a deliberate design (Amaze actually has separate view mode for landscape? I don't think so). Hmm, but returning to portrait should preserve the grid, and it doesn't — that's the bug.\n\nActually maybe the mechanism: on configuration change, the new activity reads `getSharedPreferences(\"uimode\")` which only stores the *global* view mode. Hmm.\n\nLet me report this as a bug. But first, let me reproduce cleanly once more from a known state and gather exact evidence:\n- In portrait Amaze, menu shows \"List View\" (i.e., grid active).\n- Rotate landscape: menu shows \"Grid View\" (list active) — setting lost.\n- Rotate portrait: menu shows \"Grid View\" (still list).\n\nWe have that evidence. Let me rotate back and confirm once more.\n\nActually, we've reproduced this 3 times (twice with rotations). Strong. Let me file.\n\nElement_ref: in portrait after returning, element 4 is More options; the menu item \"Grid View\" would be the evidence. But at the moment I'm in landscape with menu open showing \"Grid View\" (element 0). I'll take it as evidence: the menu offers \"Grid View\" meaning folder is in list mode after rotation from a grid-set folder.\n\nLet me rotate back first to observe the state in portrait and file with element ref of the menu. Actually I can file now using current observation (landscape menu). The quote \"Grid View\" is on screen. Good.\n\nBut the report should be about state lost on rotation. Let me write it with element_ref=0 (Grid View menu item in landscape) and quote \"Grid View\". Hmm, but the \"screen\" would be Amaze in landscape. Maybe better to rotate back to portrait, open menu, and quote \"Grid View\" there too. Both work. Let me close menu (back), rotate portrait, open menu to confirm and then file with portrait refs.\n\nActually if I open the menu, take observation, the file action will use that observation's element numbers. Let me do it."}
