o root and bookmark \"Audiobooks\"? Alphabetically Audiobooks is after AndroidQA but before DCIM. Existing: Amaze, DCIM... Adding Audiobooks: alphabetical → Amaze, Audiobooks, DCIM. Addition-append → Amaze, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures, Audiobooks. Newest-first → Audiobooks, Amaze, DCIM...\n\nLet me add Audiobooks from root. Close drawer, tap Internal Storage to go root. Then bookmark Audiobooks. Then open drawer.\n\nActually, I recall the second report was exactly this and rejected. Hmm. But now with \"Amaze\" also present, the result may be clearer. Still likely rejected.\n\nLet me step back and consider the possibility that the intended bookmark bug is the persistence/rotation issue rather than ordering. But the changed note says ordering. Perhaps the \"ordered by when they were added\" change inadvertently broke persistence? Or the ordering implementation stores only the last-added? Hmm.\n\nWait! Maybe here's the thing: \"entries are now ordered by when they were added\" — maybe the implementation stores an order index/time for each bookmark. If the implementation is buggy, adding bookmarks in a certain order could cause entries to be *missing* or *replaced*. E.g., using a SparseArray indexed by timestamp truncated, or storing in SharedPreferences with key collisions. Hmm.\n\nOur observation that 4 bookmarks vanished could be the actual planted bug: adding multiple bookmarks quickly (within the same second?) might overwrite previous ones because the order key is the timestamp with low resolution. That would be a cool bug: bookmarks added within the same second share a key and overwrite each other. Then ordering by addition time would lose entries.\n\nBut we saw all 4 present simultaneously right after adding. So no immediate overwrite.\n\nAlternatively, maybe rotating the device (activity recreate) is when they got lost. Let me test that specifically: currently \"Amaze\" bookmark exists. Rotate to landscape and back, then check drawer — does \"Amaze\"