{"type": "thinking", "text": "Whoa! Now the drawer shows: Internal Storage, AndroidQA, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures. The \"Amaze\" bookmark is GONE, and only AndroidQA remains! So adding the AndroidQA bookmark caused \"Amaze\" to disappear?! Or it replaced it.\n\nInteresting! Let me think: We added \"Amaze\" bookmark earlier, then \"AndroidQA\" bookmark. Now only \"AndroidQA\" is present — \"Amaze\" is gone. So adding a second bookmark REPLACED the previous one? Or maybe the bookmark list holds only one custom bookmark?\n\nWait, earlier we had 4 custom bookmarks simultaneously (Alpha, Beta, Audiobooks, Alarms). So multiple can coexist. Hmm.\n\nBut maybe the ordering feature (\"ordered by when added\") stores only the latest? No...\n\nHold on. Maybe the issue: The bookmark for \"Amaze\" got removed because I bookmarked AndroidQA which... no.\n\nHmm, wait. Notice the notification banner \"Found 3 retained objects grouped as 2...\" — that's a system notification, irrelevant.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe \"Amaze\" bookmark is still there but appears... no, the list is AndroidQA, DCIM,... no Amaze.\n\nSo the \"Amaze\" bookmark disappeared after adding \"AndroidQA\". That suggests bookmarks added via context menu are not accumulated properly — maybe each \"Add to Bookmarks\" REPLACES the last added custom bookmark? But earlier we had 4! Unless those 4 were all present because... hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the bookmark list stores by *key = folder name* and inserting AndroidQA overwrote... no, Amaze vs AndroidQA are different keys.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the same bookmark twice? No.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider the earlier 4: Alpha, Beta, Audiobooks, Alarms were all present. Then later they vanished. Maybe the pattern is: the app persists the LAST added bookmark only? Let's test: add another bookmark now (e.g., \"Audiobooks\") and see if AndroidQA disappears. If yes, then each add replaces the previous custom bookmark (a bug). But that contradicts the earlier 4.\n\nWait, maybe the earlier 4 vanished when the drawer was first opened after some action. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the bookmarks are stored per \"current directory\" somehow: \"Add to Bookmarks\" adds to a list associated with... no.\n\nLet me look at the order: AndroidQA is alphabetically after Amaze. If both were present, we'd see Amaze, AndroidQA, DCIM. We only see AndroidQA. So Amaze was removed.\n\nCould it be that \"Add to Bookmarks\" for AndroidQA hit the \"Amaze\" bookmark entry's pencil instead? Let me check: Before this, the previous screen was root and I tapped element 16 = properties icon of AndroidQA (at 985,1006). Then menu Element 7 = \"Add to Bookmarks\" at (822,2004). That should add AndroidQA.\n\nHmm, but maybe the drawer's bookmark list is showing only ONE custom bookmark because of the \"ordered by when added\" implementation using a Map with a single key? Unlikely.\n\nLet me test again: add \"Audiobooks\" bookmark from root and see if AndroidQA remains or gets replaced. Close drawer, tap Audiobooks properties icon, Add to Bookmarks, open drawer.\n\nCurrently drawer open at root. Close drawer. Root list still has Audiobooks at element 19 (properties) in the pre-drawer observation. But the background list may have shifted. Let me close drawer and observe."}
