{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now the drawer shows: AndroidQA, Audiobooks, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures.\n\nSo the \"Amaze\" bookmark is gone, but AndroidQA and Audiobooks are present. Interesting. So adding Audiobooks did NOT remove AndroidQA. So why did Amaze disappear when AndroidQA was added?\n\nAh wait! Maybe \"Amaze\" bookmark's name is displayed as... no.\n\nHmm, let me think: Maybe the bookmarks were: Amaze (added at ~6:44), then AndroidQA (added ~6:46). After adding AndroidQA, the drawer showed only AndroidQA (no Amaze). Now adding Audiobooks, the drawer shows AndroidQA, Audiobooks (no Amaze).\n\nCould it be that the \"Amaze\" bookmark disappeared because the app's bookmark list has a bug where bookmarks under the *current* directory are removed when you leave? Hmm. The Amaze bookmark was /storage/emulated/0/AndroidQA/Amaze. We are currently at root. Hmm.\n\nOr maybe \"Amaze\" was never actually bookmarked persistently; it appeared in the drawer right after adding (in-memory), but when we navigated away and the drawer rebuilt, it vanished. Yes! That's likely: the \"Add to Bookmarks\" adds to an in-memory list; when the drawer is refreshed (e.g., after navigating or after another add), the in-memory list gets reloaded from persistent storage (which lacks the new entries) → new bookmark disappears. But then AndroidQA and Audiobooks persist in the drawer after subsequent adds... Hmm.\n\nWait: after adding AndroidQA, we opened the drawer and saw only AndroidQA (Amaze gone). Then closed drawer, added Audiobooks, opened drawer → AndroidQA and Audiobooks. So AndroidQA persisted across an add, but Amaze didn't. What's different?\n\nMaybe the difference: When I added \"Amaze\" bookmark, the current folder was /AndroidQA (its parent). When I added \"AndroidQA\", current folder was root (its parent). Both same pattern.\n\nHmm, timing? Between adding Amaze and adding AndroidQA, we rotated landscape→portrait. Rotation recreated the activity; maybe the bookmark added before rotation was in memory only and got lost during rotation. Exactly! Sequence:\n- Added Amaze bookmark (in-memory).\n- Opened drawer (saw Amaze), closed, rotated landscape (activity recreate) → in landscape drawer, Amaze missing. So rotation lost it (in-memory not saved). Then rotated back; drawer still had no Amaze (we saw?). Actually after rotating back, we opened drawer and saw \"Amaze\" present! Wait, we DID see Amaze after rotating back at 6:46 ([17] contains \"Amaze\"). Hmm, that contradicts.\n\nLet me re-trace:\n1. Added Amaze bookmark at ~6:44 (current dir AndroidQA). Opened drawer → saw Amaze.\n2. Closed drawer.\n3. Rotated landscape (6:46) → drawer visible, NO Amaze (only DCIM...).\n4. Rotated portrait → opened drawer → Amaze PRESENT again ([17]).\n5. Closed drawer, pressed BACK to root (6:46).\n6. Added AndroidQA bookmark.\n7. Opened drawer → Amaze GONE, AndroidQA present.\n8. Closed, added Audiobooks.\n9. Opened drawer → AndroidQA, Audiobooks present; Amaze gone.\n\nHmm so Amaze disappeared after step 6/7. It was present in step 4. So adding AndroidQA removed Amaze?! Or maybe navigating from AndroidQA to root triggered a reload that dropped Amaze.\n\nThe in-memory theory: after rotation, the activity reloaded bookmarks from disk (Amaze missing but drawer showed Amaze? contradiction). Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the list is capped at N custom bookmarks? No, we had 4 earlier.\n\nWait, maybe the bookmark sort/order logic has a bug where adding a bookmark with a name that sorts *after* another causes the earlier one to be lost? Like an ordering map with wrong keys? Hmm: Amaze added first, AndroidQA added second. Both remain? No, Amaze gone.\n\nMaybe the custom bookmarks are stored keyed by *path hash* or by *name*, and \"Amaze\" collides with the app name? Hmm no.\n\nHold on — maybe the drawer shows only bookmarks that are *not* the currently displayed... no, we're at root.\n\nLet me check whether \"Amaze\" is truly gone or maybe now labeled differently. The drawer now shows AndroidQA, Audiobooks, DCIM... no Amaze.\n\nLet me verify via the \"Modify Bookmark\" mechanism: each bookmark has a pencil. Could there be more bookmarks below Pictures not shown? No, after Pictures comes Quick access.\n\nOK. There is clearly something wrong with bookmark persistence/addition. But the changed note is about ordering. Maybe the actual planted bug manifests as: adding bookmarks causes wrong ordering/loss because the implementation uses a timestamp map incorrectly.\n\nLet me try to be scientific: current bookmarks: AndroidQA (added 6:46), Audiobooks (added 6:47), plus defaults DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures.\nOrder shown: AndroidQA, Audiobooks, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures. That's alphabetical (A-n-d vs A-u-d: AndroidQA < Audiobooks yes). Also addition order: AndroidQA then Audiobooks. Both consistent.\n\nNow add \"Alarms\" (alphabetically before AndroidQA, added third). If alphabetical → Alarms, AndroidQA, Audiobooks, DCIM... If addition-append → AndroidQA, Audiobooks, DCIM, ..., Pictures, Alarms. If newest-first → Alarms, Audiobooks, AndroidQA, DCIM... Let's do it: close drawer, add Alarms bookmark, open drawer.\n\nBut before that, let me consider the \"loss\" of Amaze. To test whether it's lost when adding a new bookmark, I could first add a bookmark, verify, then add another, verify both. Currently AndroidQA + Audiobooks both present (two customs). So multiple customs persist across an add. So the Amaze loss might be due to rotation or the BACK navigation. Hmm.\n\nActually! Maybe the \"Amaze\" bookmark was never persisted and the drawer's in-memory list is rebuilt when navigating to a different directory (BACK to root). When we added Amaze while in /AndroidQA and opened the drawer, it showed the in-memory list including Amaze. Then pressing BACK to root caused MainActivity to reload/recreate the drawer list from persisted prefs (Amaze missing). That fits: the bookmark was added to an in-memory list but not persisted, and a directory navigation triggered a reload from disk.\n\nBut then AndroidQA and Audiobooks also should be lost on navigation. Unless they were persisted because... hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the bookmarks added are persisted only when the *drawer is closed* or when you navigate? Confusing.\n\nLet me test the simple persistence now: Exit the app and reopen; check whether AndroidQA and Audiobooks persist. If they do, then those two are persisted. If Amaze was lost before exit, maybe it was a one-off due to rotation.\n\nLet me do: Exit → reopen → open drawer, check.\n\nClose drawer → More options → Exit → reopen → drawer."}
