howed up in the drawer. Then I pressed BACK to root and added AndroidQA. After that, Amaze disappeared. \n\nCould the \"Amaze\" bookmark have been *overwritten* because \"AndroidQA\" has the same... no.\n\nHmm, what if the bookmarks are stored in a Map keyed by the *folder name* and the order list stores names, and \"Add to Bookmarks\" for AndroidQA inserted at the same index (e.g., index 0) replacing Amaze? But then Audiobooks and Alarms additions would replace AndroidQA, yet they coexist. Hmm.\n\nWhat if the bookmark order uses an index/time and inserting a bookmark with an *earlier alphabetical* name shifts/replaces? No.\n\nLet me look at the actual sequence of custom bookmarks:\n- 6:44: Amaze added.\n- 6:46: rotation tests; Amaze shown in portrait.\n- 6:46: BACK to root.\n- 6:46: AndroidQA added → Amaze gone, AndroidQA present.\n- 6:47: Audiobooks added → AndroidQA, Audiobooks present (2 customs).\n- 6:47: Alarms added → Alarms, AndroidQA, Audiobooks (3 customs).\n\nSo after adding AndroidQA, only 1 custom (Amaze lost). After adding Audiobooks, 2 customs. After adding Alarms, 3 customs. Maybe the \"Amaze\" bookmark was lost due to the rotation, and the drawer showing Amaze after rotating back was from the *in-memory* list that got rebuilt later? Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the rotation-to-landscape triggered saving the current bookmark list from a *different* Bookmarks instance (landscape) that didn't have Amaze, then rotating back loaded it (Amaze still shown? no).\n\nThis is too speculative. The main observable bug: added bookmarks can silently vanish, and ordering is alphabetical instead of add order. The changed note is about ordering though.\n\nLet me try a different tactic: maybe the intended bookmark bug is that after adding bookmarks, they're ordered by addition time, but the drawer displays them reversed or sorted; the dev can't reproduce because in the dev's build the bug doesn't manifest with my steps. Perhaps I need to check the ordering after a restart.