{"type": "thinking", "text": "Eureka! This confirms the bug: After choosing RENAME on a folder paste conflict (copy /Amaze/Alpha into /Amaze/Beta where Beta/Alpha already exists), the app did NOT create a renamed folder \"Alpha (1)\". Instead, it MERGED the source folder's contents directly into the existing /Amaze/Beta/Alpha folder: now Beta/Alpha contains marker.txt (original) AND readme.txt (from the source). The folder count in Beta stayed \"1 folders\" — no renamed copy was created.\n\nThis is the changed bullet #4: \"Folder copying: the contents of a renamed folder copy are now written to their destination in a new way.\" The new way writes the contents into the existing conflicting folder instead of into a new renamed folder.\n\nWait, but was this content from the source? The source /Amaze/Alpha has readme.txt (0 B). Beta/Alpha now has readme.txt (0 B) + marker.txt (0 B). Yes, readme.txt came from the source. So the rename copy's contents were merged into the destination's existing folder.\n\nHmm, but is it possible that the RENAME actually created \"Alpha (1)\" but the file list didn't update, and readme.txt appearing is a coincidence? No—readme.txt wasn't there before; it appeared after RENAME. So the copy wrote contents into Beta/Alpha.\n\nThis is the bug! And it's likely the intended one for #4 (and #2's no-op is the same manifestation). The dev confirmed #2 earlier. Now I can file a more specific report for #4 about contents being merged into the existing folder instead of a renamed copy.\n\nLet me report this with precise evidence:\n- Setup: /Amaze/Beta/Alpha contained marker.txt (renamed from readme.txt).\n- Copied /Amaze/Alpha (contains readme.txt) into /Amaze/Beta (already has Alpha).\n- Conflict dialog Alpha → RENAME.\n- Result: no new folder; /Amaze/Beta still \"1 folders and 2 files\"; /Amaze/Beta/Alpha now shows 2 files: marker.txt + readme.txt (source's contents merged into the existing folder).\n\nExpected: a new folder (e.g., \"Alpha (1)\") should be created in Beta containing readme.txt; existing Alpha should remain with marker.txt only.\n\nThis is a strong bug. Let me file it. element_ref: current observation element 6 = \"0 folders and 2 files\" in Beta/Alpha, or element 11 \"readme.txt\". I'll point at element 11 (readme.txt added) and quote \"readme.txt\". Actually the defect is the merged readme in the existing folder. Use element_ref=11 quote \"readme.txt\" and mention \"0 folders and 2 files\".\n\nLet me file."}
