{"type": "thinking", "text": "The developer says \"that one is already logged.\" So it's the same as the previously confirmed bug (folder RENAME no-op). Good — that's confirmed.\n\nNow, remaining: bullet #1 (view per path) and bullet #3 (bookmark ordering). My reports for those were rejected. Maybe the intended bugs there are different. Let me think harder.\n\nBullet #1: \"Directory view options: the list or grid choice is now stored per folder path.\"\nMaybe the bug is that the choice is stored per folder path but the storage key is wrong in a way that... We observed the view is lost on rotation/restart. That seems like the obvious bug. But rejected twice (rotation, restart). Hmm.\n\nWait — maybe the view mode IS persisted, but the *drawer* or something overrides it. Let me verify whether the view mode is stored correctly when navigating with the \"Home\" button or drawer vs BACK. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe I should test the per-folder behavior more precisely: does changing the view in folder A affect folder B? We saw Amaze grid, Alpha list, so independent. But after restarting the app, all reset to list. Maybe that's intended (view mode is per-session)? The note says \"stored per folder path\", implying persistence though. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the bug is the opposite: the view mode IS stored per path now, but the \"sort\" choice is also stored per path and interferes? No.\n\nLet me test another aspect: \"Only this folder\" checkbox in Sort By dialog. That's about sort, not view. But maybe the view mode change interacts with sort's \"Only this folder\". The changed bullet is only about view.\n\nHmm, maybe the hidden bug is: when you change the view for one folder, it changes for ALL folders of the same name? We tested Alpha (grid) and Beta/Alpha (list) — different. So per-path is right.\n\nMaybe it's the other way: the view mode is stored per *parent* path rather than folder path? No.\n\nLet me look at the view mode behavior when navigating via drawer bookmarks: tapping a bookmark might open the folder with a default view instead of its stored view. Hmm, that could be the bug: view stored per path but bookmarked navigation loses it. Hard to test but possible.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the bug is with the *first* folder visited: new folders default to grid instead of list (or vice versa). We saw Beta (never visited, opened from grid Amaze) was grid. Expected per-path default might be list. Hmm, but per-path stored means unvisited paths have no stored value; the default could legitimately be the global/last-used. So not a bug.\n\nLet me test the view mode persistence across a *simple* activity recreate without landscape: e.g., using the app's \"Exit\" then reopen we saw list. Rejected.\n\nHmm, maybe the dev's \"could not reproduce\" for the view mode report was because I described \"grid lost\" but their build actually keeps it and my device had a glitch due to the automatic \"grid/list\" being tied to the dual-pane landscape. But we saw portrait list after restart.\n\nLet me try yet another test for #1: Check if the view mode is stored per path in a way that a *renamed* folder inherits. E.g., set /Amaze/Alpha to grid, rename it to Alpha2, does Alpha2 keep grid? If stored by path, renaming creates a new path with no setting → default. That's expected.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the bug is that after setting grid for Amaze and navigating into Alpha then back, Amaze reverts to list? We saw it stayed grid (before restart). Hmm.\n\nLet me test a different usage: set view in a deep folder, then use the \"Home\" button (which might create a new tab/fragment) and come back. Or use the drawer to navigate. Perhaps the bug is that when a folder is opened via a bookmark/drawer, its stored view isn't applied.\n\nActually, maybe I should test two folders with the SAME path name to see if the stored mode collides — we did (Alpha paths differ, modes differ). Good.\n\nHmm, what about the \"grid/list stored per folder path\" across app *process restart*: We saw reset. That's likely the bug. But rejected.\n\nWait, maybe the view mode is stored in SharedPreferences under a key, and it IS persisted, but the app on fresh start defaults to list because the *file list fragment* loads before the preference? That would be flaky. The dev might not reproduce because their device's timing differs. Hmm.\n\nLet me try once more with a very clear, minimal scenario and give the dev more detail (e.g., confirm the grid remains while navigating, then restart). Maybe the earlier reports were rejected because I mentioned rotation or because of the count confusion. Let me do a clean restart test now:\n\n1. Navigate to /Amaze (currently nested). It's list now.\n2. Set Grid View.\n3. Navigate to AndroidQA (BACK) then re-open Amaze → confirm still grid (in-session persistence).\n4. Navigate to root via Home button? Then Exit.\n5. Reopen → go to Amaze → check grid/list.\n\nActually, the \"Exit\" flow returns to the same folder on reopen. Let me test with a different navigation: set grid, press HOME (not Exit), then from launcher open app (resume) → grid persists (we saw). Then use \"Exit\" → reopen → grid lost.\n\nHmm, the developer may consider \"Exit\" as a reset.\n\nAlternatively, test with process death by force-stopping via the system Settings app? That's outside Amaze but allowed? We can open Android Settings (via recents? no). We could use `open_app`? Not for settings. Hmm.\n\nActually, we can use the system Settings app if we can launch it... The tools only open the app under test. We can press HOME and tap app icons; Settings may not be on the home screen. The launcher shows Gallery, Contacts, WebView Browser Tester, Camera. No Settings.\n\nWe could use the notification shade? Not accessible via tools except swipe from top (swipe down). Maybe.\n\nThis is getting complex. Let me instead look for other bugs in sorting/directory options:\n\n- Sorting: we tested Name asc/desc, Directory Sort Mode (folders on top/files on top/none). \"Only this folder\" checkbox - let's test it. Maybe there's a bug: with \"Only this folder\" checked, the sort choice doesn't apply only to that folder or is not remembered. Or the sort direction is inverted for Size/Type.\n\n- Type sort: sort by Type. Could be a bug.\n\n- Last Modified sort: all files have same mtime (Nov 14 6:33), so hard.\n\n- Size sort: files have distinct sizes (dup_notes 15B, keep 21kB, notes 15B, photo 20kB, report 13B). Test ascending/descending size — verify order.\n\nLet me test sort by Size to check correctness. If a bug exists, the dev might confirm. The area includes \"sorting\". The changed bullet is about view per path, but sorting area is in scope. Let me test sorting thoroughly.\n\nFirst navigate to Amaze. Currently in Beta/Alpha. Press BACK twice to Amaze.\n\nActually, let me also think: Maybe the planted #1 bug is about \"sorting and directory view\" more broadly: e.g., the sort chosen in one folder leaks to another (sort \"Only this folder\" not working). Hmm.\n\nLet me test \"Only this folder\" sort:\n- Set a sort in Amaze with \"Only this folder\" checked, then check another folder's sort.\n- Then uncheck and see global.\n\nFirst, let me restore data a bit: I'll clean up later.\n\nLet me navigate to Amaze."}
