Earlier: After adding Amaze bookmark, we exited/reopened and saw the drawer had Amaze (at 6:45-ish). Wait, we did see \"Amaze\" in the drawer after Exit+reopen? Let me re-trace:\n- Added Amaze at ~6:44. Drawer showed Amaze.\n- Closed drawer. Rotated landscape → drawer (always visible) showed no Amaze. Rotated back → opened drawer → Amaze present.\n- Closed drawer, BACK to root, added AndroidQA. Opened drawer → Amaze gone, AndroidQA present.\n- Added Audiobooks → drawer: AndroidQA, Audiobooks.\n- Added Alarms → drawer: Alarms, AndroidQA, Audiobooks.\n- Exit → reopen (root 28 folders). Then navigated to Amaze/Beta/Alpha.\n- Now drawer → only defaults.\n\nSo after Exit/reopen, the customs are gone. Earlier \"Amaze survived Exit\" was wrong — we checked the drawer after Exit+reopen at 6:44? Let me scroll back: After adding Amaze, we closed drawer and did More options → Exit → reopen → then opened drawer and saw Amaze? Actually yes: \"Open drawer to check if 'Amaze' bookmark survived. ... The 'Amaze' bookmark SURVIVED the Exit/reopen!\" That was after Exit+reopen. Then rotation tests. Hmm, so it DID survive one Exit.\n\nConfusing. Unless the \"Exit\" doesn't kill the process; open_app resumes the same process with the in-memory bookmarks; then later the process got killed/recreated (e.g., after memory pressure) and the in-memory bookmarks were lost. The doubled count and lost bookmarks might both be symptoms of the app being recreated without proper state persistence.\n\nActually, the drawer at 6:45 had Amaze after Exit+reopen. Then at 6:46 we rotated, and in landscape the drawer had no Amaze; back in portrait, drawer had Amaze. Then root BACK + add AndroidQA → Amaze gone. Hmm! So the *act of adding AndroidQA* (or the BACK navigation) dropped Amaze.\n\nWait, maybe the pattern is: only the LAST N custom bookmarks are kept? Like the bookmark list is truncated to the most recent addition? At the point after adding AndroidQA: customs = {Amaze, AndroidQA} but only AndroidQA shown. After adding Audiobooks: customs shown = {AndroidQA, Audiobooks} (2!). After adding Alarms: {Alarms, AndroidQA, Audiobooks} (3!). So the count grows. Why was Amaze dropped? Maybe because \"Amaze\" bookmark is special (the app's own name?) or because adding a bookmark for a folder while its parent is the current dir... hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the bookmarks are keyed by folder NAME, and \"Amaze\" collided with... nothing.\n\nOR maybe the \"Amaze\" bookmark was removed because I tapped something? When I added AndroidQA, I tapped the properties icon of AndroidQA. Then Add to Bookmarks. Could I have accidentally opened the Modify Bookmark for \"Amaze\" and deleted? No, the flow was clear.\n\nHmm, whatever. The bigger issue: all custom bookmarks vanish after some time/restart. Let me verify a clean reproduction:\n\n1. Add a bookmark for \"Alarms\" (currently no customs).\n2. Open drawer → see Alarms.\n3. Navigate into a folder (e.g., tap Alarms bookmark? no) — press BACK? We're at Beta/Alpha. Close drawer, press BACK to Beta, BACK to Amaze.\n4. Open drawer → check if Alarms still there.\n\nIf it vanishes after navigating, we have a solid repro: \"bookmarks disappear after navigating to another folder.\"\n\nLet me test. We're in the drawer now. Close it, add Alarms bookmark (currently at Beta/Alpha; navigate to root first). Hmm, easier: the current dir is Beta/Alpha; can't bookmark Alarms without navigating.\n\nLet me navigate to root via drawer Internal Storage (tap element 20). Then add Alarms bookmark. Then navigate into Amaze (press on Alarms? no, tap Alarms row to open it) and back, then check drawer.\n\nActually simpler: add bookmark for the *current folder*? Not possible via current-dir context. We can bookmark a subfolder of the current dir: Beta/Alpha has no subfolders. Hmm.\n\nLet me go to root: tap Internal Storage (element 20)."}
