{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed! After Exit + reopen, the \"Alarms\" bookmark is GONE. The drawer shows only the defaults: Internal Storage, DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures.\n\nSo this is a solid, reproducible bug: bookmarks added via \"Add to Bookmarks\" are lost after closing and reopening the app. Wait — but earlier the \"Amaze\" bookmark seemed to survive an Exit. Maybe that was a fluke/in-memory. Let's trust this clean test:\n1. Add Alarms bookmark (root).\n2. Open drawer → Alarms present.\n3. More options → Exit.\n4. Relaunch app.\n5. Open drawer → Alarms gone.\n\nThis is a clear \"not_persisted\" bug in the bookmarks area. The changed note says \"entries are now ordered by when they were added\" — but the bigger issue is they're not saved at all. Maybe the planted bug: the new ordering feature stores entries in memory (or a new data structure) without saving to prefs, so bookmarks are lost on restart. This is plausibly the #3 bug! And my earlier ordering reports were about a different aspect.\n\nLet me report this. It's in the bookmarks area and clearly reproducible.\n\nWait, but I need to be careful: Did the Alarms bookmark maybe get lost because opening it (navigating to Alarms) somehow removed it? We checked after navigating: it was still there. Then Exit/reopen: gone. So Exit/reopen loses it.\n\nLet me reproduce once more to be sure. Add Alarms again (currently we're in Alarms folder, drawer open; close, tap Internal Storage to root, add Alarms bookmark, verify drawer, Exit, reopen, check). This takes a few steps but worth it.\n\nActually, the previous \"Amaze bookmark survived Exit\" observation might have been a different sequence where open_app didn't actually restart the process (it just resumed the activity because the app was already in background; \"Exit\" might have finished the activity but the process stayed, and open_app recreated the activity from an in-memory singleton that still had the bookmark). Then later, after more operations, the process got killed and the in-memory list reset.\n\nIn our current test, Exit may have finished the activity but the process still had in-memory bookmarks; open_app created a new activity that read from disk (lost). Hmm.\n\nRegardless, the user-facing bug is: bookmarks disappear after closing/reopening the app. Let me reproduce once more to confirm, and capture the exact steps.\n\nCurrent state: drawer open at Alarms. Close drawer. Go to root (tap Internal Storage bookmark element 14? that's within the drawer; tap it). Then add Alarms bookmark again. Then check drawer, Exit, reopen, check.\n\nActually, tapping Internal Storage in the drawer navigates to root and closes the drawer. Let me do that."}
