{"type": "text", "text": "The testing session has ended (device tools no longer respond), so I could not call `sign_off`. Here is the summary of the sweep.\n\n## Confirmed bug (developer acknowledged: \"already logged\")\n**Folder paste-conflict RENAME is broken**\n- Copy `/AndroidQA/Amaze/Alpha` → paste into `/AndroidQA/Amaze/Beta` where an `Alpha` folder already exists → `RENAME`.\n- Expected: a new renamed copy (e.g. `Alpha (1)`) with the source's `readme.txt`.\n- Observed: no renamed folder is created. Instead the source's contents are merged into the *existing* `Beta/Alpha` (it ended up with both `marker.txt` and `readme.txt`), and the folder count stayed \"1 folders\". Reproduced with a deliberately distinct `marker.txt` to prove the merge.\n\n## Filed but not confirmed before the session ended\n1. **Bookmarks not persisted** — Added `Alarms` (and earlier `Amaze`, `AndroidQA`, `Audiobooks`) via *Add to Bookmarks*; the drawer showed them, but after *More options → Exit* and relaunching, the drawer reverted to only the defaults `DCIM, Download, Movies, Music, Pictures`. The report returned \"No reply\", then the session closed.\n2. **Bookmark ordering** — Drawer entries were always in strict alphabetical order (`Alarms, AndroidQA, Audiobooks, DCIM, …`), not in the order they were added as the release note claims. Reported twice; rejected both times.\n3. **Grid/List choice not persisted** — Setting `/AndroidQA/Amaze` to Grid View was lost after device rotation and after app Exit/relaunch (menu offered \"Grid View\" again). Reported twice; rejected both times.\n4. **Folder count doubles after relaunch** — e.g. `/storage/emulated/0` shows \"28 folders and 0 files\" and `/AndroidQA/Amaze` shows \"4 folders and 10 files\" right after relaunch while only 14 / (2 folders + 5 files) exist; navigating away and back corrects it. Reported; rejected.\n\n## Verified working\n- File copy/paste (content and size preserved), file rename (empty-name validation, cancel, round-trip), folder rename, normal (non-conflicting) folder copy including nested contents.\n- Paste-conflict SKIP/OVERWRITE paths, and RENAME on a *file* conflict (correctly produced `notes (1).txt`).\n- Sorting by Name/Size ascending & descending, Directory Sort Mode (Folders on top / None on top), and \"Only this folder\" scoping.\n- Per-folder view mode independence within a session (e.g. Amaze grid while Alpha list), bookmark add/edit dialogs.\n\nGiven the confirmed folder-RENAME defect (and the still-open bookmark/view-state issues), this build should **not** be signed off. Test artifacts created during the sweep (`dup_notes.txt` in Amaze, a copied `Alpha` folder plus pasted `notes.txt` in Beta, and the `marker.txt` rename) were noted for cleanup but had not yet been removed when the session closed."}
